## What the root LICENSE covers

The root LICENSE (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 powerycy) covers only the code written
in this repository — the Skill layer and the glue code of the integrations.
The frozen Android port under `integrations/` is a derivative work of the
upstream Jev Chat assistant and carries its own LICENSE and attribution files.
It is **not** covered by the root LICENSE. The promoted Flutter implementation
translates derived logic from all three upstream ports; those attribution
obligations move into this NOTICE rather than lapsing.

Written in this repository: the repository tooling under `scripts/`, the ports
under `integrations/`, `tests/`, the root governance files (`README.md`, `NOTICE`,
`LICENSE`, `GLOSSARY.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `PRIVACY.md`, `docs/`, `.github/`), and the
local additions inside the skill payload directory described below.

## Provenance of the skill payload

`goutoujunshi/` is the skill payload: `SKILL.md`, `references/`,
`agents/openai.yaml`, `assets/reference-library-135.png`,
`scripts/memory_store.py` and `scripts/validate_skill.py`. It was copied from
[shengjidaguai-china/goutoujunshi](https://github.com/shengjidaguai-china/goutoujunshi)
and is maintained here as a fork; most of it is byte-identical to upstream and
`scripts/check_upstream.py` reports what has drifted. Same author and same MIT
licence as the root `LICENSE`, so the root licence covers it.

Upstream's own governance files (`README.md`, `README_EN.md`, `LICENSE`,
`LICENSE.zh-CN.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`,
`SECURITY.md`, `.gitignore`, `.github/*`) and its `documentation/` development
notes are deliberately **not** imported. The root `documentation/` in this
repository is app-layer material, not upstream's documentation directory.

