## Third-party components in the Flutter implementation

The Flutter implementation directly depends on the following components. Their
licences remain with their respective copyright holders:

| Component | Use | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Flutter SDK / Dart `ffi` package | Application framework and Windows shared-memory FFI | BSD-3-Clause |
| `windows-capture` 2.0.1 | Windows Graphics Capture wrapper | MIT |
| `windows` / windows-rs | Win32, WinRT and UI Automation bindings | MIT or Apache-2.0 |
| `rapidocr-core` 0.2.2 | RapidOCR-compatible detection, recognition and post-processing | Apache-2.0 |
| ONNX Runtime (`ort`) | Local inference runtime used by `rapidocr-core` | MIT |
| PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 Chinese mobile models | Offline Chinese detection and recognition | Apache-2.0 |
| `desktop_multi_window` 0.3.1 | Second Flutter engine and window messaging on Windows | MIT |
| `window_manager` 0.5.2 | Frameless, always-on-top Windows window control | MIT |
| `screen_retriever` 0.2.2 | Windows display geometry | MIT |

The Windows bridge disables `rapidocr-core`'s model-download feature. Model
files are release inputs and are never fetched while the application is
running.

